; Limit 04: no way to treat a typed value as the machine word it is.
; Blocks job 7 (and the dispatch half of job 5). The runtime's entry point is
; one piece of code linked into every program, but main returns (list int),
; int, or bool depending on the program. The C runtime receives the result as
; an l0_val and picks a writer from @l0_main_ret_kind. In L0 the result has
; exactly one static type, so entry code written for one return type does not
; check against a program whose main returns another.
;
; The first def is a program; the second is the runtime's entry point, written
; the way l0rt.c's run() is.

(def main ((input (list int))) (list int)
  input)

(def l0_entry ((input (list int))) int
  (main input))
